  "data_abstract": "Nuclear medium effects on $\\text{B}^+$ meson production are studied using the binary-collision scaled cross section ratio between events of different charged-particle multiplicities from proton-lead collisions.  Data, collected by the CMS experiment in 2016 at a nucleon-nucleon center-of-mass energy of $\\sqrt{s_{NN}} = 8.16\\,$TeV, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 175\\nbinv, were used. The scaling factors in the ratio are determined using a novel approach based on the Z$\\,\\to\\mu^{-}\\mu^{+}$ cross sections measured in the same events. The scaled ratio for $\\text{B}^+$ is consistent with unity for all event multiplicities, putting stringent constraints on nuclear modification for heavy flavor.",
